From: Asuvath MS <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LEC-IMX95: enable boot counting for OSTree rollback

Count boots in the U-Boot environment and run altbootcmd once bootlimit is
exceeded, so a deployment that fails to boot three times falls back to the
previous one. altbootcmd sets ostree_rollback, which boot.scr reads.

Counting is gated on upgrade_available, so a normal boot writes nothing to
flash. Applied only when the adlink-ostree distro is selected.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]

Signed-off-by: Asuvath MS <asuvath.monikandan@adlinktech.com>
---
--- a/configs/lec-imx95_defconfig
+++ b/configs/lec-imx95_defconfig
@@ -276,3 +276,7 @@
 CONFIG_NVME_PCI=y
 CONFIG_CMD_NVME=y
 CONFIG_CLK_IMX95_BLKCTRL=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD="setenv ostree_rollback 1; run bootcmd"
